# General Rules

- Keep solutions simple, maintainable, and production-ready.
- Avoid over-engineering and unnecessary abstractions.
- Do not duplicate logic; extract reusable modules when justified.
- Never hardcode environment-specific values or secrets.
- Design for scalability and operational clarity.
- Follow SOLID principles pragmatically.
- Prefer explicit naming and clear boundaries.
- Follow repository guidebook in `BASIC_GUIDES.md`.
- Update documentation when behavior or architecture changes.
